Hi, my comments below in green.

* Could you please confirm if this contract has already received *pre-approval in terms of financing* - or are you still considering other options? {color:#36b37e}*yes, financial part is approved?*{color}
* Given the value of this contract (800K), we’ve agreed that once [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] and I have finished reviewing it / discussing the required changes, [~accountid:6149a0e9ba1b34006ab04897] will *instruct DLA for a sanity check review*. I recommend you wait for DLA’s feedback before sharing the markup to Tetris. {color:#36b37e}*When you think we can make this happen, we haven’t sent back Tetris any response re agreement yet, and we need to finalise it in order to start construction works?* {color}
* Have you already *obtained the landlord’s authorization to perform these works?* In accordance with clause 6.1 of the lease, Bot cannot “perform any works or improvements to the Premises, whatever their nature, importance or extent, without prior written authorization from the Landlord”. {color:#36b37e}*yes*{color}
* Have you already ensure that *the works you want to carry out are in accordance with the Conditions for the Performance of Works by tenants*, contained in Annex 7 of the Lease (clause 7.2)? {color:#36b37e}*As I’ve commented in the document, we need to add Annex 7 from our lease agreement with Landloard to this agreement with Tetris, and to add following clause (if wording is ok from your side):*{color}
”{color:#36b37e}*Tetris must perform works, including special installations and finishing works, and architectural licensing project with accordance the Conditions for the Performance of Works by tenants, attaced as annex “X“ to this agreement, any fines and/or penalties arising from non-compliance with this clause will be covered by Tetris. We cannot ensure it before works will start, but we can secure ourselves by this clause (little background info - Tetris have already performed works in the building we are located and is acquainted with Landloard and rules, but better to be safe.*{color}
* You also need to ensure that the works respect the *quality levels of materials and aesthetic standards adopted by the Landlord* and you need to discuss this with the landlord (clause 7.3 of the Lease). {color:#36b37e}*yes, all good here, we will be in contact with the Landloard with regards this, and, I am approving all works performed by Tetris*{color}
* Under clause 7.3 of the Lease, *the landlord wlll pay €325.000,00 + VAT in the cost of implementation works* → So I guess that will come in deduction of the 800K?
{color:#36b37e}*No this won’t come as the deduction, this will be additional amount we will spend on construction, but Tetris have nothing to do with this, and no need to indicate this amount in the agreement with them. We will manage this clause directly with the Landloard.*{color}
* I am concerned that +*at the end of the lease, the landlord can request us gto remove all works + equipment at our exclusive expense*+ (clause 7.7) → Is it something that you have forecasted in terms of costs? {color:#36b37e}*Yes, they can, unfortunately this is market practice in Portugal, this was already discussed and confirmed, when signing Lease agreement for Portugal office.*{color}
* A copy of the insurance policy of the constructor needs to be given to the landlord.`
* Please also review clause 7 of the lease in its entirety as it is particularly relevant to the construction works and we should comply with all of it. {color:#36b37e}*Yes, I’ve reviewed it and left comments in the document, if to sum up:*{color}

*-* {color:#36b37e}*Clause 7.2 covered above.*{color}

{color:#36b37e}*- Clause 7.3 - all works Tetris will perform are reviewed by us, and we will check with Landloard, when necessary*{color}

- {color:#36b37e}*Clause 7.4. from our Lease Agreement is partly covered by clause 18.1 and 19.1, I will add additional comment directly to the document.*{color}

{color:#36b37e}*- Clause 7.5. from our Lease Agreement - we’ve already added comment in the document to Tetris in clause 1.4. (construction agreement), asking why we need to obtain licenses (as it is in current wording), as it should be Tetris. We can accompany my questions with our proposed wording, not to come back and force with this clause. I will comment in the document, but in general the idea would be to add following clause instead of 1.4 (construction agreement):*{color}

{color:#36b37e}*Tetris shall be solely responsible for obtaining the administrative authorizations, licenses or fees (as well as for the payment of any fines and/or penalties for their absence) necessary for the execution of the works and implementation of the equipment described in this Clause. The Botl and Landlord shall authorize all necessary documents for the purpose of obtaining such licenses and authorizations.*{color}

- {color:#36b37e}*Clause 7.6  from our Lease Agreement is already covered by clause 3.1 in the construction agreement.*{color}

{color:#36b37e}*Other paragraphs in clause 7 shouldn’t affect our agreement with Tetris. What do you think?*{color}

{color:#36b37e}*It would be necessary to add Annex VI - Technical Descriptive Note and Adaptation Works from our Lease agreement to the construction agreement, and add simple clause with an idea, that Tetris undertakes to take into account/comply the contents of this annex, when planning and executing works.*{color}

{color:#36b37e}*If necessary or something is not clear from my comments, I can provide more context/input during the call.*{color}


{color:#36b37e}*JIC will add this info here, as there are quite a lot of comments in the document: I am currently working on all technical details, timeline and budget with Tetris, therefore I will add final numbers, as soon as will have them, and we will add timeline and budget as annexes to this agreement.*{color}

