Why it is difficult to use boltcp for it?

{{The issue here is that due to static content, it's quite difficult to use boltcp for it, so probably as a first step it should be a static configuration.}}



Also could you please post an example of config?

[https://github.com/bolteu/sre-nginx-conf/blob/master/sites-available/internal-web-apps|https://github.com/bolteu/sre-nginx-conf/blob/master/sites-available/internal-web-apps|smart-link] this is part of Nginx configuration that is responsible for it. 

The main magic is here: 


{noformat}	if ($uri !~ "/(backend/|400.*\.html)") {
		rewrite ^/(.*)$ /aws-s3/$1;
	}
	if ($uri ~ "/backend/") {
		rewrite ^/backend/(.*)$ /upstream-discovery/$1;
	}
	include /etc/nginx/discovery-routes.conf;

	location /aws-s3/ {
		include /etc/nginx/snippets/internal-web-app-add-headers.conf;
		set $backend bolt-static-web-apps.s3-website.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com;
		error_page 404 = @fallback;
		proxy_intercept_errors on;
		proxy_set_header Host $backend;
		proxy_pass    http://$backend:80;
		rewrite       ^/aws-s3/(.*) /$host/$1 break;
	}
{noformat}

We have a strange redirect mechanism between “/“ for static content in S3 and “/backend” on access to nodejs service from beehive/admin/admin-panel. 

The difficulty here is that CP right now just generates routes based on information that is kept in ETCD. 
But here is the static URL for S3, and we don’t know where will be correct to place such information in ETCD and who should put this information to ETCD.  

So this task now to investigate how envoy will be handled with this logic and after that start to think about how to make work CP with this. 

But if someone who already quite familiar with envoy logic will participate in this, it will be super nice.

