Please find below general information on voluntary liquidation and our fee structure for the liquidation proceedings in Finland.

Main steps in voluntary liquidation (“selvitystila”) process of a limited liability company:

# Decision of a General Meeting on liquidation and liquidator(s);
# Registration of the liquidation decisions with the Finnish Trade Register;
# If necessary, preparation of financial statement for the period preceding the dissolution and audit (if required) thereof;
# Preparation of the financial accounts and annual reports during the liquidation;
# Application for public summons to the unknown creditors of the company (creditors can file claims within time limit set forth by the Trade Register, usually 3 months);
# Sending notifications to known creditors of the company and notification of mandatory insurance and social security contribution entities on the liquidation;
# Conversion of assets into cash (if any);
