*1.Whether we are removing the directors or they are resigning.*  

We are not sure what procedure should apply to this case. Could you please advise on:  

* What is the most expedient procedure to change the directorship of an entity? 

{color:#36b37e}ML: If the departure of the current directors is amicable, the quickest way to change the directorship of the company is for the prior directors to resign and for the sole equity holder of the company to subsequently elect new directors. This assumes the current directors will resign voluntarily. If this is the case, we can quickly prepare a resignation letter, but we’ll need wet ink signatures to register the resignation in Portugal. {color}

{color:#36b37e}If this is not the case, the directors can be dismissed without cause by resolution of the sole equity holder, which we may also prepare for you. However, please note that if the directors are remunerated for their duties in Portugal, they may be entitled to compensation for the damages caused by their dismissal. {color}

{color:#ff5630} BL: The departure of Martin and Markus Villig is amicable; therefore, we will go for the resignation procedure. {color}

{color:#36b37e}We note that, given that the articles of association do not state otherwise, the directors of the company are appointed for an indefinite period. Would you prefer to implement a finite term of office for the new directors? In Portugal terms of office have to last at least one year and must coincide with the calendar year (meaning that the first year of the new term of office will always end in December 31, 2022, the second year in December 31, 2023, and so on and so forth). Usually, terms are set for 3 or 4 years. {color}

{color:#36b37e}If this is something you wish to move forward with, we note that the resolution which appoints new directors can also amend the articles of association to accommodate this issue. The process will not become especially more cumbersome because of that. {color}

{color:#ff5630} BL: I would appoint the new directors for an indefinite period, but please {color}[~accountid:6017bc19dc29b4006a7f1025] {color:#ff5630}could you confirm your view on this? {color}

* What are the steps required in order to change the company directors? 

{color:#36b37e}ML: If the process is amicable, {color}

# {color:#36b37e}The current directors shall sign a letter of resignation. Customarily the letter will say that they have nothing to receive from the company, as a result of their resignation or otherwise. {color}
# {color:#36b37e}The sole equity holder (BOLT HOLDINGS OÜ) will issue a proxy letter on behalf of an individual to represent it in the resolution mentioned in 3. {color}
# {color:#36b37e}The sole equity holder’s representative shall execute a resolution: (i) acknowledging the resignation of the current directors; and (ii) electing the new directors. If you wish to implement a finite term of office, the resolution would also resolve on amending the articles of association to effect such a change. {color}
# {color:#36b37e}The new directors shall execute a letter of acceptance confirming their appointment. {color}
# {color:#36b37e}The resignation of the current directors and the appointment of the new directors shall be registered before the Commercial Registry Office. To that effect (only for the registration) a Portuguese tax number will be required (see question 2 below) {color}

{color:#36b37e}If the current directors will not voluntarily resign, step 1 will obviously not apply, and step 3 would read: “The sole equity holder’s representative shall execute a resolution: {color}{color:#36b37e}_(i) dismissing the current directors_{color}{color:#36b37e} and (ii) electing the new directors. (…)” {color}

{color:#36b37e}Accordingly, step 5 would include the registration of the {color}{color:#36b37e}_dismissal_{color}{color:#36b37e} (instead of resignation) of the current directors and the appointment of the new directors.{color} 

* What documents/information do you need from us? 

{color:#36b37e}ML: We are available to prepare the relevant documentation needed to effect the change, meaning (1) the letters of resignation (in case the process is amicable), (2) the proxy letter, (3) the sole equity holder’s resolution appointing the new directors and acknowledging the resignation of the current directors/dismissing them without cause (as applicable) and (4) the letters of acceptance. {color}

{color:#36b37e}In order to do so, we will need the following information: {color}

§  {color:#36b37e}  Full name and address of the appointed directors; {color}

{color:#ff5630}BL: Ahto’s address is Tamme tänav 6, 76911 Hüüru küla Saue vald Harju maakond. Could you please ask Mahmoud for his address and full name? {color}

§  {color:#36b37e}  Identity of the sole equity holder’s representative. {color}

{color:#ff5630}BL: Who should be this representative, any employee for instance? How involved does this representative need to be (i.e. signing documents, doing paperwork in person, etc.) {color}

* What is the expected timeline? 

{color:#36b37e}Once we receive the requested information, we can prepare steps 1 to 4 above and send them to you for signing in 2-3 business days. {color}

{color:#36b37e}The minutes should be printed directly onto the minutes book; please confirm if we can request such a book directly from your accounting service providers. {color}

{color:#36b37e} Once we receive the documentation signed, we will submit the modifications to the directorship for registration. This may take 1-2 business days (if you choose an urgent submission, which entails registration fees of around € 400) or around 5 business days (if you do not, in which case fees shall amount to around € 200). Additional fees are due if you also wish to amend the articles of association to implement a finite term of office. {color}

  

*2. Whether or not the new Directors have a Portuguese tax number.* 

The new directors do not have Portuguese tax numbers. Is it a key requirement that they have this as we are unsure if the existing directors have a Portuguese tax number? If so could you please obtain the Portuguese tax numbers for them? 

{color:#36b37e}ML: In order to proceed with the registration of the appointment of the new directors before the commercial registry office, the latter must have a Portuguese tax number, which we can procure before the Tax Authorities. Please note that, for internal purposes, the appointment of the directors is valid and effective (i.e. the new directors represent the company as of their appointment even if they do not have a tax number in Portugal). Registration is required for external purposes only (i.e. for enforceability against third parties). {color}

{color:#36b37e}In order to obtain a tax number, we will need: {color}

* {color:#36b37e}to see their passports or identification documents (or be provided with a certified copy thereto. Note that if the certifying entity is not Portuguese, the copy should be apostilled or legalized, depending on the jurisdiction), {color}

