However, such change may result in consequences provided by Estonian law.

 All contracts concluded under Estonian law are subject to Law of Obligations Act [https://www.riigiteataja.ee/en/eli/506112013011/consolide|https://www.riigiteataja.ee/en/eli/506112013011/consolide|smart-link] 

According to article *§ 42.*  Invalidity of standard terms: 

 29) provides the party supplying the term with the right to terminate the contract without giving reasons for the termination if the same right is not provided to the other party;

33) provides the party supplying the term with the right to terminate a contract entered into for an unspecified term without good reason and without a reasonable period of advance notice;

Article *§ 186.*  Bases for extinction of obligation provides the following:

  An obligation extinguishes:

* by an agreement to terminate the obligation;
* upon withdrawal from the contract;
* upon cancellation of the contract;

Articles *§* 188 -194 provide terms for withdrawal from the contract (TBD with [~accountid:5f0ea3c39d9a1200294cef2c])

Articles *§*195 -196 provide terms for cancellation of contract (TBD with [~accountid:5f0ea3c39d9a1200294cef2c])

